# Rust build artifacts (crates/xtask don't exist until Phase 0, but this
# applies from the first `cargo build`)
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# Working notes that are deliberately local-only, and that `AGENTS.md` already
# describes as ignored: "`docs/superpowers/plans/`, `docs/audits/`, and
# `docs/scratch/` hold the phase-by-phase implementation plans, audit findings,
# and scratch notes — they exist locally but are gitignored, so don't expect
# them on a fresh clone." Until now that sentence was simply false; these four
# lines make it true.
#
# This is a safety property and not tidiness. Untracked directories of this
# size sit directly in `git add -A`'s path: one such command swept 60k+ lines
# of ledger into a commit during Subsystem D, and recovering from it cost more
# than the work it interrupted. `docs/architecture/` is the *frozen design* and
# stays tracked — only these three subtrees are local.
docs/superpowers/
docs/audits/
docs/scratch/
# The orchestration ledger (task briefs, reports, sweep output, `progress.md`).
# Same class as the three above: local working state for the agent run, not
# part of the repository's history.
.superpowers/
